{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">2013 CEMC Cayley #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">2013 CEMC Fermat #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A large cylinder can hold <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/5/c35439c4a81c53a93ab2838ad0ed043925461270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\text{ L}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> of chocolate milk when full.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33dd1ba16c1f5976b67c5bcb38984e5a108f2430.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(100); pen lightGray= rgb(&quot;B2AFAC&quot;);  defaultpen(linewidth(0.8bp));  path area  = (0,0) -- (2,0) -- (2, 2.9) -- (0,2.9) -- cycle;  filldraw(area, lightGray);  draw((0,4)--(0,0)--(2,0)--(2,4));  draw((0,4)--(-1/6,4)); draw((0,3)--(-1/6,3)); draw((0,2)--(-1/6,2)); draw((0,1)--(-1/6,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"92\" height=\"168\" />\nThe tick marks show the division of the cylinder into four parts of equal volume. Which of the following is the best estimate for the volume of chocolate milk in the cylinder as shown?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5ba50bb50fe800b932b147adb665a4ec27b2be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 24 \\text { L} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 28 \\text { L} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 30 \\text { L} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 36 \\text { L} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40 \\text { L}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"476\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Based on the diagram, the amount of chocolate milk in the container approximately reaches the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />rd tick mark. Because the tick marks divide the cylinder into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> parts,the cyclinder is about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5549fc0dbc6bc60d0f34d60fe07b0476c15c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}\\text{ths}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"38\" /> full.\n</p><p>Thus, the volume of the chocolate milk in the cylinder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df10ae62dc0d40ad87279ebcc1e1cde74fb21c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\times \\frac{3}{4} = 37.5 \\text{ L}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>However, we can see from the diagram that the actual amount of chocolate milk is slightly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tick marks up. The only answer choice that is slightly below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c19a57d56318e83eb4b0b8cf8d13f3a81abb7f6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37.5 \\text{ L}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc57d06c5f2e422aed6d3af6ce04db127468c95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 36 \\text { L}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"83\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Ca